1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:03,820
The SAT gives you a math reference sheet.

2
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:06,340
But it mostly covers shapes.

3
00:00:06,360 --> 00:00:10,580
Algebra and advanced math are about
seventy percent of the section,

4
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:13,569
and almost none of their
formulas are on it.

5
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:14,850
Those are on you.

6
00:00:15,315 --> 00:00:17,415
First, here's exactly
what is on the sheet,

7
00:00:17,435 --> 00:00:20,085
so you don't waste time memorizing it.

8
00:00:20,235 --> 00:00:26,925
Then, fifteen formulas that aren't,
each with a quick SAT-style example.

9
00:00:27,388 --> 00:00:28,958
Here's the whole sheet.

10
00:00:29,268 --> 00:00:32,048
Area and circumference of a circle.

11
00:00:32,068 --> 00:00:35,158
Area of a rectangle and a triangle.

12
00:00:35,228 --> 00:00:39,128
The Pythagorean theorem, and
the two special right triangles:

13
00:00:39,148 --> 00:00:42,648
thirty, sixty, ninety, and forty-five,

14
00:00:42,668 --> 00:00:44,558
forty-five, ninety.

15
00:00:45,022 --> 00:00:48,602
Volumes of a rectangular prism, cylinder,

16
00:00:48,622 --> 00:00:50,642
sphere, cone, and pyramid.

17
00:00:50,662 --> 00:00:55,202
And three facts: a circle has
three hundred sixty degrees,

18
00:00:55,222 --> 00:01:01,082
or two pi radians, of arc, and a triangle's
angles add up to one hundred eighty

19
00:01:01,102 --> 00:01:02,102
degrees.

20
00:01:02,622 --> 00:01:03,242
That's all of it.

21
00:01:03,262 --> 00:01:04,841
Look those up when you need them.

22
00:01:04,861 --> 00:01:07,312
Everything else, you need to know cold.

23
00:01:07,822 --> 00:01:09,642
Part one, lines.

24
00:01:09,662 --> 00:01:13,122
Formula one is slope: y two minus y one,

25
00:01:13,142 --> 00:01:15,522
over x two minus x one.

26
00:01:15,542 --> 00:01:16,992
Rise over run.

27
00:01:17,417 --> 00:01:18,547
Example.

28
00:01:19,297 --> 00:01:22,517
A line passes through
the points negative two,

29
00:01:22,537 --> 00:01:25,677
seven, and four, negative five.

30
00:01:25,697 --> 00:01:28,027
What is the slope of the line?

31
00:01:28,467 --> 00:01:30,077
Pause and try it.

32
00:01:34,878 --> 00:01:37,777
The change in y is
negative five minus seven,

33
00:01:37,797 --> 00:01:39,288
or negative twelve.

34
00:01:39,718 --> 00:01:42,817
The change in x is four
minus negative two,

35
00:01:42,837 --> 00:01:44,248
or six.

36
00:01:44,558 --> 00:01:47,658
Negative twelve over six is negative two.

37
00:01:47,678 --> 00:01:49,287
The answer is A.

38
00:01:49,780 --> 00:01:52,240
The traps are flipping
it to run over rise,

39
00:01:52,260 --> 00:01:54,510
and losing a negative sign.

40
00:01:54,660 --> 00:01:57,790
Subtract in the same
order on top and bottom.

41
00:01:58,235 --> 00:02:01,014
Formula two is three forms of a line.

42
00:02:01,034 --> 00:02:05,095
Slope-intercept: y equals m x plus b,

43
00:02:05,115 --> 00:02:08,614
where m is the slope and
b is the y intercept.

44
00:02:08,634 --> 00:02:13,895
Point-slope: y minus y one
equals m times x minus x one,

45
00:02:13,915 --> 00:02:16,605
for when you know a point and the slope.

46
00:02:17,124 --> 00:02:22,054
And standard form: A x plus B y equals C.

47
00:02:22,164 --> 00:02:25,413
Its slope is negative A over B.

48
00:02:25,842 --> 00:02:26,782
Example.

49
00:02:26,802 --> 00:02:31,422
A line has a slope of four and
passes through the point three,

50
00:02:31,442 --> 00:02:32,382
one.

51
00:02:32,402 --> 00:02:35,972
What is the y coordinate
of its y intercept?

52
00:02:36,455 --> 00:02:38,065
Pause and try it.

53
00:02:42,867 --> 00:02:44,047
Use point-slope.

54
00:02:44,067 --> 00:02:48,287
y minus one equals four
times x minus three.

55
00:02:48,307 --> 00:02:52,406
That's y minus one equals
four x minus twelve,

56
00:02:52,426 --> 00:02:55,717
so y equals four x minus eleven.

57
00:02:56,026 --> 00:02:58,596
The y intercept is negative eleven.

58
00:02:59,016 --> 00:03:00,276
Formula three.

59
00:03:00,296 --> 00:03:02,915
Parallel lines have equal slopes.

60
00:03:02,935 --> 00:03:06,556
Perpendicular lines have
negative reciprocal slopes:

61
00:03:06,576 --> 00:03:09,306
flip the fraction and change the sign.

62
00:03:09,783 --> 00:03:10,923
Example.

63
00:03:10,943 --> 00:03:16,633
Line p is defined by six x
minus two y equals seven.

64
00:03:16,783 --> 00:03:20,242
Line q is perpendicular to line p.

65
00:03:20,262 --> 00:03:22,633
What is the slope of line q?

66
00:03:23,103 --> 00:03:24,713
Pause and try it.

67
00:03:29,514 --> 00:03:34,934
Line p is in standard form, so
its slope is negative A over B:

68
00:03:34,954 --> 00:03:38,694
negative six over negative
two, which is three.

69
00:03:38,714 --> 00:03:42,323
Flip it and change the
sign: negative one third.

70
00:03:42,474 --> 00:03:44,323
The answer is B.

71
00:03:44,772 --> 00:03:46,752
Three is the parallel slope.

72
00:03:46,772 --> 00:03:51,702
Negative three and positive one
third each do only half the job.

73
00:03:52,146 --> 00:03:53,396
Formula four.

74
00:03:53,666 --> 00:03:57,276
Distance is the square
root of the change in x,

75
00:03:57,346 --> 00:04:00,085
squared, plus the change in y, squared.

76
00:04:00,105 --> 00:04:02,236
That's just the Pythagorean theorem.

77
00:04:02,305 --> 00:04:06,516
And the midpoint averages the
x values and the y values.

78
00:04:06,967 --> 00:04:07,977
Example.

79
00:04:08,247 --> 00:04:12,547
Segment A B has endpoints
A at negative one,

80
00:04:12,567 --> 00:04:15,657
two, and B at five, ten.

81
00:04:15,887 --> 00:04:18,657
What is the length of segment A B?

82
00:04:19,087 --> 00:04:20,697
Pause and try it.

83
00:04:25,499 --> 00:04:27,039
The changes are six and eight.

84
00:04:27,059 --> 00:04:29,358
Six squared plus eight
squared is one hundred,

85
00:04:29,378 --> 00:04:31,799
and the square root of one hundred is ten.

86
00:04:31,819 --> 00:04:34,189
The midpoint is two, six.

87
00:04:34,721 --> 00:04:38,781
In Desmos, type distance, with
the two points in parentheses,

88
00:04:38,801 --> 00:04:40,171
and you get ten.

89
00:04:40,881 --> 00:04:43,010
Midpoint works the same way.

90
00:04:43,431 --> 00:04:45,561
Part two, quadratics.

91
00:04:46,230 --> 00:04:52,601
Formula five: for a x squared
plus b x plus c equals zero,

92
00:04:52,631 --> 00:04:59,611
x equals negative b, plus or minus the
square root of b squared minus four a c,

93
00:04:59,631 --> 00:05:01,401
all over two a.

94
00:05:01,838 --> 00:05:02,898
Example.

95
00:05:02,918 --> 00:05:08,578
Which of the following are the solutions
to two x squared minus four x minus

96
00:05:08,598 --> 00:05:10,247
three equals zero?

97
00:05:10,702 --> 00:05:12,312
Pause and try it.

98
00:05:18,113 --> 00:05:22,653
a is two, b is negative four,
and c is negative three.

99
00:05:22,673 --> 00:05:25,413
Under the root: sixteen plus twenty-four,

100
00:05:25,433 --> 00:05:26,652
which is forty.

101
00:05:26,672 --> 00:05:30,373
So x equals four, plus
or minus root forty,

102
00:05:30,393 --> 00:05:31,522
over four.

103
00:05:31,962 --> 00:05:34,252
Root forty is two root ten.

104
00:05:34,321 --> 00:05:38,902
Divide every term by two:
two, plus or minus root ten,

105
00:05:38,922 --> 00:05:39,901
over two.

106
00:05:39,921 --> 00:05:41,572
The answer is C.

107
00:05:42,162 --> 00:05:47,332
D forgot to divide by two a, and A
used negative four for negative b.

108
00:05:47,787 --> 00:05:52,487
Formula six is the discriminant:
b squared minus four a c.

109
00:05:52,507 --> 00:05:54,767
Positive means two real solutions.

110
00:05:54,787 --> 00:05:56,807
Zero means exactly one.

111
00:05:56,827 --> 00:05:58,596
Negative means none.

112
00:05:59,053 --> 00:06:00,183
Example.

113
00:06:00,813 --> 00:06:05,513
In the equation x squared
plus ten x plus c equals zero,

114
00:06:05,533 --> 00:06:07,023
c is a constant.

115
00:06:07,612 --> 00:06:11,432
If the equation has
exactly one real solution,

116
00:06:11,452 --> 00:06:13,343
what is the value of c?

117
00:06:13,763 --> 00:06:15,373
Pause and try it.

118
00:06:20,174 --> 00:06:24,143
Exactly one solution means
the discriminant is zero.

119
00:06:24,374 --> 00:06:27,194
One hundred minus four c equals zero,

120
00:06:27,214 --> 00:06:29,264
so c is twenty-five.

121
00:06:29,806 --> 00:06:34,986
Desmos shortcut: graph y equals
x squared plus ten x plus c,

122
00:06:35,006 --> 00:06:37,186
and add a slider for c.

123
00:06:37,206 --> 00:06:40,986
The slider only runs from
negative ten to ten at first,

124
00:06:41,006 --> 00:06:43,386
so change its upper limit to fifty.

125
00:06:43,406 --> 00:06:46,986
Then drag until the parabola
just touches the x axis.

126
00:06:47,006 --> 00:06:48,496
That's at twenty-five.

127
00:06:49,066 --> 00:06:51,285
Formula seven is the vertex.

128
00:06:51,305 --> 00:06:55,676
Its x coordinate is negative b over two a.

129
00:06:55,706 --> 00:06:57,406
Plug that in to get y.

130
00:06:57,426 --> 00:07:02,486
And in vertex form, y
equals a times x minus h,

131
00:07:02,506 --> 00:07:06,166
squared, plus k, the vertex is just h,

132
00:07:06,186 --> 00:07:07,186
k.

133
00:07:07,292 --> 00:07:08,392
Example.

134
00:07:08,412 --> 00:07:14,672
What is the vertex of the graph of y
equals two x squared plus twelve x plus

135
00:07:14,692 --> 00:07:15,701
thirteen?

136
00:07:16,166 --> 00:07:17,776
Pause and try it.

137
00:07:23,577 --> 00:07:26,836
Negative twelve over
four is negative three.

138
00:07:26,856 --> 00:07:32,796
Plug it in: eighteen minus thirty-six
plus thirteen is negative five.

139
00:07:32,816 --> 00:07:36,237
The vertex is negative
three, negative five.

140
00:07:36,257 --> 00:07:38,027
The answer is D.

141
00:07:38,480 --> 00:07:42,569
Desmos check: graph it and
click the bottom of the curve.

142
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:45,290
Desmos labels the vertex for you.

143
00:07:45,741 --> 00:07:51,481
Formula eight: for a x squared
plus b x plus c equals zero,

144
00:07:51,501 --> 00:07:54,401
the sum of the solutions
is negative b over a,

145
00:07:54,421 --> 00:07:57,711
and the product is c over a.

146
00:07:57,820 --> 00:07:59,271
No solving needed.

147
00:07:59,749 --> 00:08:00,839
Example.

148
00:08:01,269 --> 00:08:08,368
What is the product of the solutions
to two x squared plus nine x minus ten

149
00:08:08,388 --> 00:08:09,638
equals zero?

150
00:08:10,067 --> 00:08:11,677
Pause and try it.

151
00:08:16,479 --> 00:08:20,859
c over a is negative ten over
two, which is negative five.

152
00:08:20,879 --> 00:08:22,329
The answer is B.

153
00:08:22,439 --> 00:08:28,009
Negative nine halves is the sum, and
negative ten forgot to divide by a.

154
00:08:28,422 --> 00:08:31,312
Part three, circles and trig.

155
00:08:31,701 --> 00:08:36,682
Formula nine: x minus h,
squared, plus y minus k,

156
00:08:36,702 --> 00:08:39,311
squared, equals r squared.

157
00:08:39,342 --> 00:08:43,712
The center is h, k, and the radius is r.

158
00:08:43,862 --> 00:08:47,352
If the equation comes
expanded, complete the square.

159
00:08:47,774 --> 00:08:48,904
Example.

160
00:08:49,014 --> 00:08:54,474
The equation x squared plus y squared
plus eight x minus two y equals eight

161
00:08:54,494 --> 00:08:57,423
represents a circle in the x y plane.

162
00:08:57,454 --> 00:08:59,624
What is the radius of the circle?

163
00:09:00,064 --> 00:09:01,674
Pause and try it.

164
00:09:07,476 --> 00:09:11,966
Half of eight is four, and
four squared is sixteen.

165
00:09:12,076 --> 00:09:14,656
Half of negative two is negative one,

166
00:09:14,676 --> 00:09:16,766
and that squared is one.

167
00:09:16,875 --> 00:09:19,566
Add sixteen and one to both sides.

168
00:09:20,037 --> 00:09:23,936
Now it's x plus four,
squared, plus y minus one,

169
00:09:23,956 --> 00:09:25,777
squared, equals twenty-five.

170
00:09:25,797 --> 00:09:29,096
The radius is five, not twenty-five.

171
00:09:29,116 --> 00:09:33,057
The answer is C, and the
center is negative four,

172
00:09:33,077 --> 00:09:34,077
one.

173
00:09:34,247 --> 00:09:35,457
Formula ten.

174
00:09:36,447 --> 00:09:39,907
Arcs and sectors are
fractions of the circle.

175
00:09:39,927 --> 00:09:43,827
The fraction is the central
angle over three sixty.

176
00:09:43,847 --> 00:09:47,027
Multiply it by the
circumference for arc length,

177
00:09:47,047 --> 00:09:49,976
or by the area for sector area.

178
00:09:50,397 --> 00:09:51,567
Example.

179
00:09:51,717 --> 00:09:55,127
A circle has a radius of nine centimeters.

180
00:09:55,157 --> 00:09:58,577
What is the area, in square centimeters,

181
00:09:58,597 --> 00:10:02,327
of a sector with a central
angle of forty degrees?

182
00:10:02,817 --> 00:10:04,427
Pause and try it.

183
00:10:09,229 --> 00:10:11,409
Forty over three sixty is one ninth.

184
00:10:11,429 --> 00:10:15,609
The whole area is eighty-one
pi, so the sector is nine pi.

185
00:10:15,629 --> 00:10:17,248
The answer is B.

186
00:10:17,268 --> 00:10:21,038
Two pi is the arc length,
which is the common mix-up.

187
00:10:21,579 --> 00:10:25,269
If the angle is in radians,
compare it to two pi instead.

188
00:10:25,695 --> 00:10:27,265
Formula eleven.

189
00:10:27,934 --> 00:10:32,905
Soh-cah-toa: sine is
opposite over hypotenuse,

190
00:10:32,975 --> 00:10:39,275
cosine is adjacent over hypotenuse,
and tangent is opposite over adjacent.

191
00:10:39,295 --> 00:10:42,385
Always measured from the
angle the question names.

192
00:10:42,829 --> 00:10:43,879
Example.

193
00:10:44,029 --> 00:10:49,919
In right triangle X Y Z,
angle Z is the right angle.

194
00:10:50,109 --> 00:10:56,799
X Z is twenty-four, Y Z is
seven, and X Y is twenty-five.

195
00:10:56,988 --> 00:10:59,919
What is the value of cosine of X?

196
00:11:00,388 --> 00:11:01,998
Pause and try it.

197
00:11:06,799 --> 00:11:10,529
From angle X, the adjacent
side is twenty-four,

198
00:11:10,718 --> 00:11:13,329
and the hypotenuse is twenty-five.

199
00:11:13,399 --> 00:11:17,018
So cosine of X is
twenty-four over twenty-five.

200
00:11:17,038 --> 00:11:18,659
The answer is C.

201
00:11:18,679 --> 00:11:22,208
Seven over twenty-five is sine of X.

202
00:11:22,647 --> 00:11:28,307
Now notice: from angle Y, sine is
also twenty-four over twenty-five.

203
00:11:28,327 --> 00:11:29,587
That's the rule.

204
00:11:29,607 --> 00:11:34,706
Sine of x equals cosine
of ninety degrees minus x,

205
00:11:34,726 --> 00:11:37,976
because the two acute
angles add up to ninety.

206
00:11:38,431 --> 00:11:39,571
Example.

207
00:11:39,591 --> 00:11:44,931
If sine of x degrees equals
cosine of thirty-two degrees,

208
00:11:44,951 --> 00:11:50,401
and x is between zero and
ninety, what is the value of x?

209
00:11:50,873 --> 00:11:52,483
Pause and try it.

210
00:11:57,284 --> 00:11:59,824
Ninety minus thirty-two is fifty-eight.

211
00:11:59,844 --> 00:12:04,544
To check in Desmos, switch
to degrees in graph settings,

212
00:12:04,564 --> 00:12:09,533
then type sine of fifty-eight
and cosine of thirty-two.

213
00:12:09,683 --> 00:12:10,894
Same decimal.

214
00:12:11,339 --> 00:12:13,509
Part four, exponents.

215
00:12:13,539 --> 00:12:15,999
Formula twelve is a set of rules.

216
00:12:16,019 --> 00:12:18,199
Multiplying, add the exponents.

217
00:12:18,219 --> 00:12:19,958
Dividing, subtract them.

218
00:12:19,978 --> 00:12:22,199
Power of a power, multiply them.

219
00:12:22,219 --> 00:12:24,748
A negative exponent means one over.

220
00:12:24,898 --> 00:12:29,669
And in a fraction exponent, the top is
the power and the bottom is the root.

221
00:12:30,142 --> 00:12:31,232
Example.

222
00:12:31,382 --> 00:12:37,482
Which expression is equivalent to
the quantity three x to the fourth,

223
00:12:37,502 --> 00:12:40,802
squared, times x to the negative five,

224
00:12:40,822 --> 00:12:42,832
where x is not zero?

225
00:12:43,224 --> 00:12:44,834
Pause and try it.

226
00:12:50,635 --> 00:12:53,414
Squaring gives nine x to the eighth.

227
00:12:53,434 --> 00:12:56,175
Then multiply by x to the negative five,

228
00:12:56,195 --> 00:13:00,455
so add the exponents:
eight minus five is three.

229
00:13:00,475 --> 00:13:02,284
That's nine x cubed.

230
00:13:02,515 --> 00:13:04,325
The answer is A.

231
00:13:04,634 --> 00:13:07,965
C doubled the three
instead of squaring it.

232
00:13:08,405 --> 00:13:09,855
Formula thirteen.

233
00:13:10,045 --> 00:13:15,745
Growth: y equals a times
the quantity one plus r,

234
00:13:15,765 --> 00:13:16,814
to the t.

235
00:13:16,964 --> 00:13:19,464
For decay, it's one minus r.

236
00:13:19,484 --> 00:13:23,814
a is the starting amount, and
r is the percent as a decimal.

237
00:13:24,246 --> 00:13:25,416
Example.

238
00:13:25,446 --> 00:13:28,706
A machine was worth five thousand
dollars when it was bought,

239
00:13:28,726 --> 00:13:32,586
and its value decreases
by ten percent each year.

240
00:13:32,606 --> 00:13:36,106
Which function gives
its value V, in dollars,

241
00:13:36,126 --> 00:13:38,176
t years after it was bought?

242
00:13:38,695 --> 00:13:40,305
Pause and try it.

243
00:13:45,106 --> 00:13:48,126
Losing ten percent means
keeping ninety percent,

244
00:13:48,146 --> 00:13:50,446
so the multiplier is point nine.

245
00:13:50,466 --> 00:13:52,756
The answer is D.

246
00:13:53,026 --> 00:13:56,405
B keeps only ten percent, C is growth,

247
00:13:56,425 --> 00:13:58,236
and A is linear.

248
00:13:58,643 --> 00:14:03,783
After two years, the machine is
worth four thousand fifty dollars,

249
00:14:03,803 --> 00:14:05,253
not four thousand.

250
00:14:05,283 --> 00:14:08,782
Each year takes ten percent
of a smaller amount.

251
00:14:08,802 --> 00:14:13,022
In Desmos, use x for t, define f of x,

252
00:14:13,042 --> 00:14:15,613
and type f of two to check.

253
00:14:16,053 --> 00:14:19,222
Part five, percents and stats.

254
00:14:19,372 --> 00:14:23,913
Formula fourteen: percent
change is new minus old,

255
00:14:23,933 --> 00:14:26,512
over old, times one hundred.

256
00:14:26,532 --> 00:14:30,473
From forty dollars to
thirty-four is a six-dollar drop,

257
00:14:30,493 --> 00:14:34,663
and six over forty is a
fifteen percent decrease.

258
00:14:35,199 --> 00:14:37,739
The SAT also runs it backward.

259
00:14:37,759 --> 00:14:38,969
Example.

260
00:14:38,998 --> 00:14:44,059
After a twenty percent discount, a
jacket costs forty-eight dollars.

261
00:14:44,079 --> 00:14:46,729
What was the original price of the jacket?

262
00:14:47,247 --> 00:14:48,857
Pause and try it.

263
00:14:54,658 --> 00:14:57,428
Twenty percent off means
you pay eighty percent.

264
00:14:57,577 --> 00:14:59,958
Point eight times the
price is forty-eight,

265
00:14:59,978 --> 00:15:01,838
so the price is sixty dollars.

266
00:15:01,858 --> 00:15:03,268
The answer is C.

267
00:15:03,726 --> 00:15:06,746
The trap is B, adding twenty
percent of forty-eight.

268
00:15:06,766 --> 00:15:10,906
But the discount came
off the original price,

269
00:15:10,926 --> 00:15:12,615
not the sale price.

270
00:15:13,126 --> 00:15:17,816
Formula fifteen: the mean is
the sum divided by the count.

271
00:15:18,246 --> 00:15:24,256
The version the SAT really wants
is total equals mean times count.

272
00:15:24,687 --> 00:15:25,667
Example.

273
00:15:25,687 --> 00:15:28,947
The mean of a student's five
test scores is eighty-two.

274
00:15:28,967 --> 00:15:34,666
What score on a sixth test would make
the mean of all six scores equal to

275
00:15:34,686 --> 00:15:35,686
eighty-four?

276
00:15:36,171 --> 00:15:37,781
Pause and try it.

277
00:15:43,582 --> 00:15:48,192
Five scores averaging eighty-two
total four hundred ten.

278
00:15:48,222 --> 00:15:52,911
Six scores averaging eighty-four
total five hundred four.

279
00:15:53,182 --> 00:15:55,311
The difference is ninety-four.

280
00:15:55,542 --> 00:15:58,121
Whenever values are added or removed,

281
00:15:58,141 --> 00:15:59,592
switch to totals.

282
00:16:00,031 --> 00:16:03,770
On test day, trigger words
tell you which formula to use.

283
00:16:03,790 --> 00:16:06,371
Perpendicular: negative reciprocal.

284
00:16:06,391 --> 00:16:09,440
Exactly one solution: discriminant.

285
00:16:09,590 --> 00:16:13,811
Sum or product of the
solutions: negative b over a,

286
00:16:13,831 --> 00:16:15,330
or c over a.

287
00:16:15,350 --> 00:16:18,001
Maximum or minimum: vertex.

288
00:16:18,454 --> 00:16:21,394
Center or radius: complete the square.

289
00:16:21,414 --> 00:16:24,754
Percent per year: one plus or minus r,

290
00:16:24,774 --> 00:16:25,784
to the t.

291
00:16:26,054 --> 00:16:28,954
A mean with a value added or removed:

292
00:16:28,974 --> 00:16:29,794
totals.

293
00:16:29,814 --> 00:16:32,863
And if it's on the reference
sheet, just open the sheet.

294
00:16:33,305 --> 00:16:34,965
That's all fifteen on one screen.

295
00:16:34,985 --> 00:16:36,995
Pause here if you want a screenshot.

296
00:16:37,386 --> 00:16:40,966
Every example here was
written for this video,

297
00:16:40,986 --> 00:16:43,676
in the style of the real test.

298
